{{/*
  delegation-context — the standard "Session context for delegation"
  preamble that lets a prompt hand off work to child conversations via
  `mitto_conversation_new` / `mitto_conversation_send_prompt`.

  Renders the running session's ID (used as `self_id` in every `mitto_*`
  tool call), the workspace's configured ACP-server catalog, and the
  currently-existing children (when any). The children section is
  emitted only when `.Children.AllText` is non-empty so an empty
  workspace does not print a stray "Existing children:" heading.

  Consumers: code/cleanup-code, code/optimize, code/refactor,
  code/simplify, ci/fix-ci, ci/fix-errors.

  Usage — parameter-less; renders against the ambient
  *PromptEnabledContext so `.Session`, `.ACP`, and `.Children` resolve:

      {{ template "_shared/delegation-context" . }}

  The fragment uses only `.` accessors and no funcs, so it is safe to
  attach to every render context (target.title paths included).
*/}}
